  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q61-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "61",
    "prompt": "Given $\\tan\\alpha=\\dfrac{b\\sin\\beta}{a+b\\cos\\beta}$, show that\n$$\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)=\\frac{a\\sin\\beta}{b+a\\cos\\beta}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)=\\dfrac{a\\sin\\beta}{b+a\\cos\\beta}$.\n\nSubstitute the given $\\tan\\alpha$ into the tangent difference formula and simplify using $\\sin^2\\beta+\\cos^2\\beta=1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)&=\\frac{\\tan\\beta-\\tan\\alpha}{1+\\tan\\beta\\tan\\alpha}\\\\\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)&=\\frac{\\dfrac{\\sin\\beta}{\\cos\\beta}-\\dfrac{b\\sin\\beta}{a+b\\cos\\beta}}{1+\\dfrac{\\sin\\beta}{\\cos\\beta}\\dfrac{b\\sin\\beta}{a+b\\cos\\beta}}\\\\\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)&=\\frac{\\sin\\beta(a+b\\cos\\beta)-b\\sin\\beta\\cos\\beta}{\\cos\\beta(a+b\\cos\\beta)+b\\sin^2\\beta}\\\\\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)&=\\frac{a\\sin\\beta}{a\\cos\\beta+b(\\cos^2\\beta+\\sin^2\\beta)}\\\\\\tan(\\beta-\\alpha)&=\\frac{a\\sin\\beta}{b+a\\cos\\beta}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
